/-!
# Self-audit B6 (probe Bsa3): witnesses for shard B's 10-27 files the audit did not cover

Notes: `formal/notes/B-self-audit3.md` (verdict table, mutants under `formal/lean/Wip/Bsa3/`).

## §1-§2. `RigSrc.gcd_rig_first_env` is jointly satisfiable, with a real latch

Audit row (824f130): "joint non-vacuity UNVERIFIED". `RigSrc`'s own witness `W.env_nonvacuous`
covers the env lap alone, not the env together with C's 367-operator network.

* §1 `cell_sh1`: shifting a run one tick to the left (C's `shiftRun 1`) preserves every
  NON-source cell model, provided every request and acknowledge is low at tick 0. C's
  `cell_rt` needs `φ 0 = 0` and so cannot do this; here each reset field at tick 1 is
  derived from that cell's own step relation at tick 0 (all inputs low there).
* §2 the run. `Y` (data in `SelfAuditB6Data`, generated by an untrusted scratch simulator) is
  a unit-delay run of C's gcd_hw network (a = 12, b = 18) with the RIG environment: the three
  source requests are one trace `e` (bd_fork wires), `e` = C(out0.ack, ¬k) (uenv1),
  `k` = C3 of the three source acks (the fork's c3), out0.ack = C(out0.req, ¬e) (uenv0).
  Step 0 of `Y` is the reset step (only the three source requests rise), and `chS =
  shiftRun 1 Y` is the run in C's rig convention (tick 0 = release, `start.req` high).
  The kernel checks: every non-source operator meets C's `Cell` (`kChk`), every channel is
  `Held`, H_FORK_WIRE, H_DAT, H_REL, H_REL0, H_OUT0_ACK, H_UENV1_B, H_C3, M1, M0 with every
  read map `id`. `rig_env_feeds` passes all of them to `gcd_rig_first_env` itself, and out0
  latches at tick 474 with value 6 (`rig_env_latch`).

  Assumed: nothing (this is a satisfiability result). Proved: the hypotheses of
  `gcd_rig_first_env` hold together in one run in which out0 latches gcd 12 18 = 6, and the
  env starts its second offer (e re-rises at tick 432) before out0's ack falls.
  NOT covered: other inputs, other schedules, non-unit delays, non-identity read maps (all
  wire/pin reads in the witness are zero-delay), anything about silicon.

## §3. `ResetGcdNetR5` (not in the audit): a run for `re_reset_binary`

`r5_reset_witness`: the unit-delay simulation of the R5 network from the ALL-ZERO power-up
state, with rst held 1 and every data input 0, meets `Bounded 0 0` and H_RST_HELD; so the
theorem applies and gives the reset values from tick 23 on. Not degenerate in the state
(node 287, a reset-1 arbiter state, starts at 0), but degenerate in the delays (D = W = 0,
unit delay). NOT covered: D, W > 0; `re_reset_release` (H_FRONT_HOLD) not witnessed here.
-/

